01:39:51 | INFO | 🤖 Target initial answer: The reason people with bald heads can still grow thick beards comes down to a fascinating biological paradox involving hormones and genetics. Here is the breakdown of why this happens: **1. The Main Culprit: DHT (Dihydrotestosterone)** Both hair loss and beard growth are driven by the same hormone: **DHT**. DHT is a highly active form of testosterone. When testosterone circulates in the body, an enzyme converts some of it into DHT. This hormone then binds to receptors in your hair follicles. **2. The Paradoxical Effect** Here is where the weird biology kicks in. Hair follicles on different parts of the body react to DHT in completely opposite ways: * **On the scalp:** In people who are genetically predisposed to male pattern baldness (androgenetic alopecia), the hair follicles on the top of the head are highly sensitive to DHT. When DHT binds to these follicles, it causes them to shrink (a process called miniaturization). Over time, the hair gets thinner and shorter until the follicle stops producing hair entirely. * **On the face:** The hair follicles on the face (as well as the chest and back) have the exact opposite reaction. DHT actually **stimulates** these follicles. It is the hormone responsible for turning light "peach fuzz" into thick, dark beard hair during and after puberty. **3. Different Genetic "Blueprints"** You might wonder why follicles on the same head react so differently to the exact same hormone. It is because hair follicles act like independent mini-organs, and they have different genetic programming depending on where they are located. * The follicles on the top of the head are genetically programmed to view DHT as a threat (if you have the baldness gene). * The follicles on the face, and even on the sides and back of the head, are genetically programmed to view DHT as a growth signal. **The Result** Because high levels of DHT (or a high sensitivity to it) cause both scalp hair loss and beard hair growth, it is incredibly common to see men with completely bald heads and massive, thick beards. The very hormone that is shutting down the hair factories on top of their head is working overtime to fertilize the hair factories on their face.
